; regression test for a false-rejection bug found while auditing forall-intro's
; soundness check (`eval_done`'s `not_allowed` computation, see doc/kurt-soundness.md):
; a predicate symbol whose *first use* happens to be inside a `let` block used to be
; wrongly treated as a fresh individual local to that block (just like a genuine
; `const`/`let`/`pick`-introduced object would be), and so was wrongly forbidden from
; appearing in the block's forall-intro conclusion, even though it never actually
; depended on the block's own fresh constant. `P` here is only ever mentioned inside
; `let x`, on purpose.
load logic
bool P
arity P 1
let x
    use P x
    P x
true
